+`config` contains only saved selections and is empty on a fresh install. `proposal` exposes all 13 roles with unresolved model slots. Scalar roles have one initial slot, and panels or pools have three. No exact model is a proposal default. Missing roles execute on the actual native Claude parent with their original cardinality and `source: "unconfigured"`. Disclose that resolution. Before-setup tasks remain available.
+
+On a rerun, retain independently chosen models, executors, aliases, efforts, list order, and duplicates. A retired role in the saved file, such as `how explorer` or `why investigators`, appears in `droppedRoles` and not in `config`. Show each one to the user. The next save drops it. Other unknown role keys fail validation without changing preferences.
+
+## 5. Select the budget and role mapping
+
+Use a budget already specified in the conversation. Otherwise show the saved budget, or explain that `large` keeps each role's starting effort, and offer the original four choices. Each role has a target effort, which is its starting effort moved by the budget. `large` keeps it, `unlimited` raises it one step, `medium` lowers it one step, and `small` lowers it two steps, on the ladder `max` > `xhigh` > `high` > `medium` > `low`. A target at either end of the ladder stays there. `hardest tasks` starts at `max`. `reflect tooling`, `swarm workers`, the three panels, and the cross-judge pool start at `high`. The other roles start at `xhigh`, and each budget label names where those land.
+
+- `unlimited` names `max` reasoning.
+- `large` names `xhigh` reasoning.
+- `medium` names `high` reasoning.
+- `small` names `medium` reasoning.
+
+Run `scripts/models.mjs budget --budget LABEL --catalog ABSOLUTE_CATALOG` to preview the highest supported effort at or below each role's target. It retains exact model IDs, executors, role shapes, list order, duplicates, and aliases. Parent aliases keep the actual parent's settings. Resolve unsupported saved choices before saving. Do not persist unresolved proposal slots. A user may leave roles unconfigured after seeing their parent fallback.
+
+Show every role's current and proposed executor, exact model, and effort. Ask whether to accept the proposal or change specific roles. Offer the detected choices and parent aliases. Honor choices already authorized in the conversation. A user can choose one available model for several roles without editing each role manually.
+
+Scalar roles hold one entry or parent alias. `arena runners`, `architect runners`, and `interrogate reviewers` hold nonempty lists. Run one independent delegate per entry, including duplicates and aliases. `arena cross-judge pool` is an ordered candidate pool, from which Arena runs one eligible judge from a vendor other than the parent's. Families are the ones Phase A of the arena skill defines, so Fable is its own family. Fable and the other Claude models are one vendor. Parent aliases never judge. Preserve Arena's ordered selected pool and disclosed judge skip, plus every other workflow's original diversity, verifier, retry, and fresh-worker requirements.
+
+Antigravity choices retain `{ "executor": "antigravity", "model": "EXACT_AGY_ID", "reasoningEffort": "LEVEL" }`. They have no provider or authentication fields and create no native model definitions. Budget previews keep the exact ID and use only that model's reported efforts. A fixed `xhigh` variant has no lower effort unless its per-model evidence says otherwise. If the target cannot be met, resolve `needsChoice` without silently switching IDs. Follow [Antigravity execution](../poteto-mode/references/agy-execution.md) for scoped permissions, complete context, native history, exact continuation, and capability limits.
+
+## 6. Review, register, and save
+
+Show accepted roles, remaining unconfigured roles, budget, and evidence sources. Write the accepted sparse config to an absolute temporary JSON file. Validate it with `scripts/models.mjs write --input ABSOLUTE_JSON --catalog ABSOLUTE_CATALOG --expected-hash HASH --dry-run`. Use the read hash, or `absent` if no file exists. Missing roles keep their disclosed native-parent fallback.
+
+Run `scripts/register-agents.mjs --input ABSOLUTE_JSON`. It derives four native agent kinds from this plugin's original bodies for each distinct exact Claude model. It writes owned definitions under the Claude home, without editing the installed plugin cache, unrelated agents, `settings.json`, or Codex configuration. `general-purpose`, `poteto-agent`, and `comment-sicko` retain their supplied bodies. `read-only` retains the general-purpose body and disallows `Write`, `Edit`, and `NotebookEdit` for actual readonly callers. Bash remains available. Task-specific effort uses the native invocation parameter.
+
+Registration retains earlier owned variants so interruption or a rejected preference save leaves the saved selection usable. The receipt lists these unused files in `retained`. Registration never prunes them, including on later reruns, because another setup may still save a staged choice. Explicit unregister removes all owned variants.
+
+Registration is idempotent. Updates and older plugin bundles refresh the proposed variants from their bundled bodies and retain other owned variants unchanged. A modified or unowned destination produces a conflict before registration changes. An interrupted registration retains a journal and completes that same transaction on the next run. Preserve the diagnostic files if recovery reports a user edit.
+
+After registration succeeds, run the same `models.mjs write` command without `--dry-run`. A changed hash requires reloading the current choices before saving. The helper saves atomically and leaves identical bytes untouched.
+
+## 7. Finish setup
+
+Report the preferences path, selected executors, registered exact-model definitions, and detected CLI versions. State which choices came from a catalog or manual confirmation. A saved preference or definition does not verify execution. Explain that a new Claude Code session refreshes the registered agent list when needed. When the user requests execution verification, use the selected executor binding and effort. Native Claude workers use the emitted `agentType` and the installed namespace for a small task with the selected worker. Keep observed model identity separate from requested settings. Distinguish fixture checks, native CLI execution, and Desktop UI evidence. A helper-only check does not establish first-time onboarding.
